{
  "id": 231558428,
  "iid": 11150,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Draft: epan: Fix setting addr and port on wildcarded conversation",
  "description": "When a conversation lookup not using address B or port B succeeds,\nwe can try to set the second address or port on the found conversation\nif 1) the search lookup *had* an address B or port B, but we weren't\nusing it for that lookup, and 2) the found conversation *didn't* have\na second address or port.\n\nThe second test is done inside conversation_set_[addr,port]2.\nThe first test is done in find_conversation, but it was accidentally\nlooking if the *found conversation* had an address or port 2.\nThis also meant that the port or address setting in those cases\nnever happened, because first the found conversation was tested\nif it had a address or port 2, and then if it didn't yet.",
  "state": "opened",
